0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#what-ships-and-what-this-page-supplies","title":"What ships, and what this page supplies"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-reaction-time-budget","title":"The reaction-time budget"},{"depth":2,"url":"#five-gaps-you-close-first","title":"Five gaps you close first"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-health-endpoint-does-less-than-you-expect","title":"The health endpoint does less than you expect"},{"depth":2,"url":"#readiness-is-a-different-question","title":"Readiness is a different question"},{"depth":2,"url":"#build-the-deployment","title":"Build the deployment"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-this-deployment-does-not-do","title":"What this deployment does not do"},{"depth":2,"url":"#when-it-doesnt-work","title":"When it doesn't work"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"An autoscaling reference deployment"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"The complete Kubernetes deployment that scales workers on queue depth without a human in the loop: every manifest, the reaction-time budget nobody publishes, and the five gaps in the shipped examples you have to close first."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," you have run ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/scaling-workers","children":"scaling workers"}]," and\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/scaling-cas","children":"scaling the CAS"}]," by hand, you trust the numbers, and you\nwant the pool to size itself. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," a worker\ndeployment that grows and shrinks on queue depth, with probes, drain, and\ndisruption budgets wired up. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," a day to assemble, a week of watching\nbefore you trust it."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Workers and a CAS you have already sized by hand."}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The two scaling pages tell you ",["$","em",null,{"children":"what"}]," to scale on and ",["$","em",null,{"children":"why"}],". This page is the\ndeployment: the manifests, the config changes they depend on, and the latency\nbetween a build backing up and a pod existing."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-brand/40 bg-brand-soft/40 text-foreground","role":"note","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M12 16v-4M12 8h.01M12 22c5.523 0 10-4.477 10-10S17.523 2 12 2 2 6.477 2 12s4.477 10 10 10Z"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"Kubernetes deployments ship with Enterprise"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The Helm charts for running Forge on Kubernetes are part of\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"https://enterprise.forge.com","children":"Forge Enterprise"}],". What follows is the\nreference for assembling worker autoscaling yourself on top of the Kustomize\nbuilding blocks this repository ships."]}]]}]]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-ships-and-what-this-page-supplies","children":"What ships, and what this page supplies"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Being blunt about this up front, because it changes how you read everything\nbelow."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The repository contains no autoscaling artifacts for Forge."}]," It has\nno ","$L8",", no KEDA ","$L9",", no VPA, and no metrics\nadapter configuration for any Forge workload. The one HPA in the tree\nscales the OpenTelemetry collector, and the one ","$La"," protects\nthe same collector. Neither has anything to do with your workers."]}],"\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38"]}],"$L39"]}],["$L3a","$L3b"],"$L3c"]}],"isPartial":"$@3d","staleTime":"$3e","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L3f","isPartial":"$@40","staleTime":"$3e","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L41","isPartial":"$@42","staleTime":"$3e","varyParams":"$43"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@44","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@45"}
