27:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"/status"}]," answers whether the components that registered a health indicator\nhave failed. It stays ",["$","code",null,{"children":"200"}]," while a component is still initializing, which is\nthe right answer for a liveness probe and the wrong one for readiness. The\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"health"}]," service therefore also serves ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/ready"}]," (",["$","code",null,{"children":"readiness_path"}],", default\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"/ready"}],"), which answers ",["$","code",null,{"children":"503"}]," while anything is initializing or failed and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"200"}]," otherwise."]}]
28:["$","p",null,{"children":["For a worker, the component that matters is its registration with the\nscheduler. Each worker registers a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"workers/<name>"}]," indicator that reads\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"Initializing"}]," until the scheduler has answered its ",["$","code",null,{"children":"connect_worker"}]," with a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"ConnectionResult"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Ok"}]," while that connection holds, and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Initializing"}],"\nagain after it is lost and the worker is reconnecting, so only ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/ready"}],"\ndrops: a liveness probe on ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/status"}]," stays green through a scheduler roll\ninstead of restarting every worker. A Kubernetes readiness probe on the\nworker's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/ready"}]," turns the pod Ready when the worker can take work rather\nthan when its container started, and turns it not Ready again if it loses\nthe scheduler. Anything that reads pod readiness, an autoscaler's idle clock\nincluded, then counts from registration."]}]
