36:["$","$L54",null,{"children":[["$","$L55",null,{"title":"The HPA reports `unable to fetch metrics` for the external metric","id":"the-hpa-reports-unable-to-fetch-metrics-for-the-external-metric","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Work backwards along the chain. Query the recording rule in Prometheus directly;\nif it returns nothing, the problem is upstream of Kubernetes entirely and the\nadapter is fine. If the rule returns data but the adapter doesn't, the usual\ncause is the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"resources.overrides"}]," block: external metrics still need a\nnamespace association, and a series with no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"namespace"}]," label cannot be matched\nto one. Add a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"namespace"}]," label in the recording rule or via collector\nattributes."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"The pool scales up long after the build has started","id":"the-pool-scales-up-long-after-the-build-has-started","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Sum the reaction-time budget for your actual configuration. The two defaults\nthat dominate are the 60-second OTLP export interval and the 60-second interval\non the shipped ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge_performance"}]," rule group. If you skipped step 1, those\ntwo alone put you two minutes behind."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Replicas oscillate (up, down, up) during one build","id":"replicas-oscillate--up-down-up--during-one-build","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Almost always a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"scaleDown"}]," stabilization window that is too short relative to\nhow bursty the graph is. Large builds have natural lulls between phases;\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"scaleDown.stabilizationWindowSeconds: 600"}]," exists to ride through them. If it\nstill oscillates at ten minutes, the target ",["$","code",null,{"children":"averageValue"}]," is close to your\nsteady-state backlog, so small changes cross the threshold in both directions.\nRaise the target."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Scale-in produces a burst of retried actions every time","id":"scale-in-produces-a-burst-of-retried-actions-every-time","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"preStop"}]," hook is not resolving a worker id. Check that ",["$","code",null,{"children":"POD_NAME"}]," reaches\nthe config: with the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"$${POD_NAME:-worker}"}]," form above, a missing variable\nfalls back to the literal default rather than failing loudly, and every worker\nends up with the same prefix. Confirm by looking at the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"execution_worker_id"}]," label values in\nPrometheus: they should each begin with a distinct pod name."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Workers restart repeatedly under load with no obvious error","id":"workers-restart-repeatedly-under-load-with-no-obvious-error","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The liveness probe. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/status"}]," on a process whose registered leaf store is\nmemory, S3 or Azure does a full write, has and read round trip per store, and\nunder load that queues behind real traffic; each check is also cut off at\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"HealthConfig.timeout_seconds"}]," (default 5 s) and reported as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"timeout"}],", which\nthe endpoint turns into a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"503"}],". With ",["$","code",null,{"children":"periodSeconds: 30"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"failureThreshold: 4"}]," you have two minutes of grace; anything much tighter\nkills healthy workers whose only problem is a congested store. Lower\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"global.default_digest_size_health_check"}]," from its one-megabyte default as\nwell. (A worker on the shipped configs registers no indicator at all, so if\nits probe fails the process itself is not answering.)"]}]}],"$L56","$L57","$L58","$L59"]}]
