eshold"}]," turns a slow restart into a crash loop."]}]]}]
56:["$","$L55",null,{"title":"The readiness probe passes but builds fail against that pod","id":"the-readiness-probe-passes-but-builds-fail-against-that-pod","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Expected, if the store at the top of the composition is a wrapper. An\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"existence_cache"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"completeness_checking"}]," at the top registers no health\nindicator, the report is empty, and the endpoint returns ",["$","code",null,{"children":"200"}]," regardless of\nwhat is underneath. Either accept the probe as a liveness check only, or restructure\nso that a leaf store (or a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cache_metrics"}]," wrapper, which forwards registration)\nsits where the registry will see it."]}]}]
57:["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Pods are `Pending` while the queue keeps growing","id":"pods-are-pending-while-the-queue-keeps-growing","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The HPA is doing its job and the cluster has no room. Check the node autoscaler\nand whether ",["$","code",null,{"children":"resources.requests"}]," on the worker fits the instance types it can\nprovision. A worker requesting four CPUs and 8 GiB will never schedule on a\ntwo-CPU node pool, and the HPA has no visibility into that."]}]}]
58:["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Scale-down never happens even when the pool is idle","id":"scale-down-never-happens-even-when-the-pool-is-idle","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check whether the metric is going to zero or merely to a small non-zero value.\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge_execution_active_count"}]," is an up-down counter; a stuck or abandoned\noperation can leave a queued action counted indefinitely, which pins the HPA\nabove ",["$","code",null,{"children":"minReplicas"}],". Compare the metric against the actual scheduler state before\nassuming the policy is wrong."]}]}]
59:["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Everything works in staging and the adapter fails in production","id":"everything-works-in-staging-and-the-adapter-fails-in-production","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Usually multiple instance names. The shipped recording rule sums by\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}],", so a cluster serving several instances produces several series,\nand an adapter rule without an aggregation returns an ambiguous match. The\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"max(<<.Series>>{<<.LabelMatchers>>})"}]," in the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"metricsQuery"}]," above collapses\nthem; if you want per-instance pools, give each its own HPA and select on\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}]," in the label matchers instead."]}]}]
